      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Five Days One Summer (1982)** (1982) stands as one of Fred Zinnemann's final directorial works, bringing his meticulous eye to the Swiss Alps in this haunting tale of forbidden love and mountaineering drama. Like his earlier masterpiece **High Noon** (1952), Zinnemann creates intense psychological tension, but here against the backdrop of towering peaks rather than dusty streets. The film showcases Sean Connery in an unusually complex role as Douglas Meredith, a middle-aged doctor vacationing with his young companion Kate, marking a significant departure from his James Bond persona."
      },
